# LF EVERYWHERE, ON EVERY OS. Measured on the first Windows CI run (2026-11-06): with git's
# default core.autocrlf=true on the runner, checkouts got CRLF, and that broke four things at once
# -- vitest failed to parse shebang .mjs scripts it imports, the golden screens compared unequal,
# the trace fixtures changed their bytes, and a regex that finds the Action union stopped
# matching. Nothing in this project wants CRLF, and the published tarballs must not carry it.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.bin binary
*.sha256 -text
*.trace -text
*.bdf -text
